{"id": 2340929, "name": "Bell vs. Wheeler", "name_abbreviation": "Bell v. Wheeler", "decision_date": "1871-04", "docket_number": "", "first_page": "104", "last_page": "105", "citations": [{"type": "official", "cite": "3 S.C. 104"}], "court": {"name_abbreviation": "S.C.", "id": 8894, "name": "Supreme Court of South Carolina"}, "jurisdiction": {"id": 59, "name_long": "South Carolina", "name": "S.C."}, "cites_to": [], "analysis": {"cardinality": 99, "char_count": 1229, "ocr_confidence": 0.451, "pagerank": {"raw": 7.317852702137001e-08, "percentile": 0.4366069218707345}, "sha256": "73ff4d557abc02bfae86cfc04180a5cdc23181e298254d40625002dc35e344f6", "simhash": "1:836b49b1b9adc4d8", "word_count": 217}, "last_updated": "2023-07-14T20:18:05.633546+00:00", "provenance": {"date_added": "2019-08-29", "source": "Harvard", "batch": "2018"}, "casebody": {"judges": ["Wright, A. J., concurred.", "Moses, C. J., absent at the hearing."], "parties": ["Bell vs. Wheeler."], "opinions": [{"text": "The opinion of the Court was delivered by\nWillard, A. J.\nA motion is made to 'dismiss this appeal on the ground that it had not been perfected by the execution of an undertaking on the part of the appellant, as required by Sec. 359 of the Code of Procedure.\nThat Section provides that, \u201c to render an appeal effectual for any purpose,\u201d an undertaking for the payment of the costs on the appeal, to the extent of three hundred dollars, must be executed on the part of the appellant, with sureties, or that sum deposited with the Clerk. It appears that the appellant did not comply with either of these requirements. The effect of that Section, under these circumstances, is to render the appeal void and ineffectual for any purpose. The appeal must be dismissed.\nWright, A. J., concurred.\nMoses, C. J., absent at the hearing.", "type": "majority", "author": "Willard, A. J."}], "attorneys": ["McAKley & Braviley, for the motion.", "Smith & Wilson, contra."], "corrections": "", "head_matter": "HEARD APRIL TERM, 1871.\nBell vs. Wheeler.\nAn appeal not perfected by the execution of an undertaking, or a deposit of money, as security for the costs of the appeal, as required by Sec. 359 of the Code of Procedure, dismissed.\nThis was a preliminary motion to dismiss the appeal, in this case, on the ground stated in the opinion of the Court.\nMcAKley & Braviley, for the motion.\nSmith & Wilson, contra."}, "file_name": "0104-01", "first_page_order": 112, "last_page_order": 113}